    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0822" n="726" xml:id="pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Blake</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-16T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                                1926—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Referring to telegram No. 60 of August 15, 1 p.m., from the Ambassador in
                    Spain to the Department concerning Spanish control of the Tangier Zone.</p>
                <p>Please report by wire such cases as involve Spanish sphere of influence,
                    settlement of which should be required by this Government before recognizing the
                    Spanish protectorate in that area as it exists now.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d425-f1"/> Also a brief statement of such further safeguards as, in
                    your judgment, should be prerequisites to recognition.</p>
                <p>It should not be divulged that Spain has approached this Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d425-f1" n="8" xml:id="d425-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence previously printed concerning the attitude of the United
                    States on the subject of the Spanish Zone in Morocco, see <ref
                        target="frus1917#pg_1095"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1917, pp. 1095</ref>–<ref target="frus1917#pg_1096">1096</ref>; also <ref
                        target="frus1923v02#pg_585"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1923, vol.
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 585</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
